8:12Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"a0db2bd7893b71fe5bcd8462ae8ac20d9807f600","github_link":"https://github.com/MatterHackers/agg-sharp/commit/a0db2bd7893b71fe5bcd8462ae8ac20d9807f600","commit_subject":"The rich markdown editor looks like a normal WYSIWYG editor: a one-line <div align=\"center\">text</div> (or <p align>, <h1>-<h6 align>) with only an align attribute and inline content reads as an aligned paragraph or heading, written back byte-identical while untouched (the line lives on its one-member group; the block's own source stays its markdown, \"## Title\" for a heading, so a clean heading split off by Enter stays a heading) and in the regenerated <div align> wrapper form once edited, and the viewer shows the one-line div form as it already showed <p align>. Bullets are drawn shapes by depth (filled dot, hollow dot, small square) rather than \"-\", saved markers unchanged; links take the theme accent pushed to 4.5 contrast on the background; the Italic button's \"I\" is slanted; a list's last item takes a paragraph's 12 below, so a list no longer runs into the paragraph or list after it; code and table-stripe shading are the text colour at alpha 24, visible on dark themes too, and the viewer stripes tables at the same 24 so Help and Edit match. DropDownList's arrow occluder is now stacked vector layers instead of a pre-rendered gradient image, which a field at a fractional position resampled into dark lines inside its border; the layers ramp to opaque in the fill's colour over a DeviceScale-scaled distance","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"microscope-dev/microscope","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-02T00:28:04Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"4644b23e7a03151a601cdce1d26d02f5cd168b50","github_link":"https://github.com/microscope-dev/microscope/commit/4644b23e7a03151a601cdce1d26d02f5cd168b50","commit_subject":"Move breakpoints to code, name threads, and step over calls","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"commonfabric/labs","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-02T00:28:03Z",